.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_REG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_reg_count \- number of currently-registered ccol_event_reg handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

size_t ccol_event_loop_reg_count(ccol_event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the number of live registrations, meaning
ccol_event_loop_add() calls whose registration has not been removed
yet. It does not count entries in the epoll interest list, so one fd
registered for both directions counts as 2: two independent
ccol_event_reg handles stand behind it, even though they share one
entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop to query.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The number of registrations, or (size_t)-1 when loop is
CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_NULL, a stale handle, or a handle that has already
been destroyed.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call at the same time as ccol_event_loop_add(),
ccol_event_loop_remove() and a dispatch on any reactor thread. The
value is a consistent snapshot read with a single atomic load, which
cannot tear, and no lock is taken.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3)
